-- title:
--   Cyclic subrepresentations, the row-tabloid module and the real structure of the word space
-- statement:
--   For $n\in\mathbb{N}$ write $[n]=\{0,1,\dots,n-1\}$ and let $S_n$ be the symmetric group on $[n]$. A *word* of length $n$ over the alphabet $[d]$ is a map $a:[n]\to[d]$, and $W_{n,d}=\mathbb{C}^{[d]^n}$ is the space of complex functions on words, with standard basis vectors $e_a$ (the indicator function of the word $a$), so that $W_{n,d}\cong(\mathbb{C}^d)^{\otimes n}$. The group $S_n$ acts on $W_{n,d}$ by permuting positions, $(\rho_{n,d}(g)x)(a)=x(a\circ g)$; equivalently $\rho_{n,d}(g)e_a=e_{a\circ g^{-1}}$.
--
--   A Young diagram $\mu$ is a finite set of cells $(i,j)\in\mathbb{N}^2$ (row $i$, column $j$, both counted from $0$) that is closed under decreasing either coordinate; $\ell(\mu)$ denotes its number of rows. A tableau of shape $\mu$ on $n=|\mu|$ positions is a bijection $t:[n]\to\mu$. Its row word $r_t:[n]\to[\ell(\mu)]$ sends $i$ to the row index of $t(i)$, its column group $C_t\le S_n$ consists of the permutations $g$ such that $t(g(i))$ lies in the same column as $t(i)$ for every $i$, and its polytabloid is
--   $$
--   e_t=\sum_{g\in C_t}\operatorname{sgn}(g)\,\rho_{n,\ell(\mu)}(g)\,e_{r_t}\in W_{n,\ell(\mu)} .
--   $$
--   The Specht module $S^t\subseteq W_{n,\ell(\mu)}$ is the span of the $S_n$-orbit $\{\rho_{n,\ell(\mu)}(g)e_t:g\in S_n\}$.
--
--   For a group $G$, a complex representation $\rho$ of $G$ on $V$ and a vector $v\in V$, the cyclic subrepresentation generated by $v$ is $\langle v\rangle_\rho=\operatorname{span}_{\mathbb{C}}\{\rho(g)v:g\in G\}$; thus $S^t=\langle e_t\rangle_{\rho_{n,\ell(\mu)}}$. The file provides:
--
--   1. **Cyclic subrepresentations.** For every group $G$, representation $\rho$ on $V$ and $v\in V$: $v\in\langle v\rangle_\rho$, and for every subrepresentation $P\subseteq V$,
--   $$
--   \langle v\rangle_\rho\subseteq P\iff v\in P .
--   $$
--   2. **Row-tabloid module.** For a tableau $t$ of shape $\mu$, the subrepresentation $M^t=\langle e_{r_t}\rangle_{\rho_{n,\ell(\mu)}}\subseteq W_{n,\ell(\mu)}$. Since $\rho(g)e_{r_t}=e_{r_t\circ g^{-1}}$, it is spanned by the vectors $e_a$ for the words $a$ that are rearrangements of $r_t$ (letter $i$ used exactly as often as row $i$ has cells); such words encode row tabloids, so $M^t$ is the permutation module on tabloids of shape $\mu$, and $e_t\in M^t$.
--   3. **Complex conjugation.** Writing $\bar x(a)=\overline{x(a)}$, conjugation commutes with the action, $\overline{\rho_{n,d}(g)x}=\rho_{n,d}(g)\bar x$; every polytabloid is real, $\overline{e_t}=e_t$; and if $\bar v=v$ then $\langle v\rangle_{\rho_{n,d}}$ is closed under conjugation.
--   4. **Position permutations of words.** For $g\in S_n$, the bijection $a\mapsto a\circ g$ of $[d]^n$, with inverse $a\mapsto a\circ g^{-1}$.
--   5. **Invariant bilinear pairing.** For the coordinate pairing $\langle x,y\rangle=\sum_{a\in[d]^n}x(a)\,y(a)$ (no conjugation) one has, for all $g\in S_n$ and $x,y\in W_{n,d}$,
--   $$
--   \langle\rho_{n,d}(g)x,\,y\rangle=\langle x,\,\rho_{n,d}(g^{-1})y\rangle .
--   $$
--   6. **Nested subrepresentations.** If $U\subseteq V$ is a subrepresentation of $\rho$ and $S$ is a subrepresentation of the restricted representation on $U$, then the image of $S$ under the inclusion $U\hookrightarrow V$ is a subrepresentation of $\rho$.
--
--   These are the tools for the irreducibility of Specht modules in the surrounding development: together with the behaviour of the column antisymmetrizer on $M^t$, the invariant pairing and complex conjugation are used to show that every nonzero vector of $S^t$ generates $S^t$, so that $S^t$ is an irreducible representation.
--
--   **Formalization Note** The operation `cyclic` (from the base definitions of the challenge) is `Submodule.span` of the orbit, packaged as a `Subrepresentation`; conjugation is `star` and the pairing is `dotProduct` on `WordSpace n d`. The defined objects are `tabloidSub`, `wordPerm` and `subrepAmbient`; the remaining entries are the lemmas `mem_cyclic`, `cyclic_le`, `wordRep_star`, `polytabloid_real`, `cyclic_star` and `wordPair_move`.
